WEBVTT

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.410
When will you die?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:24.920
When... will you die?

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.810
Don't be shy. Come visit me more often.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.810
Your father's worried about you too, you know?

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.560
Okay.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:48.730
Please continue to take good care of Haruka...

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:53.030
I guess I'll be causing you trouble for saying something like that, right?

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:57.160
H-Hey, Mom! What are you saying?!

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:06.290
Oh, yes. There's something I want to give you two.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.290
I'll send it as soon as-

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.340
I can't hear a word you're saying.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.760
I wonder what she wants to give us...

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.730
Something appeared? You mean a ghost?

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:29.730
Um... please don't write about this in your newspaper.

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.650
Of course I won't write about this.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:35.990
Only I happen to know someone who's rather knowledgeable about that field...

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.610
Well, in that case...

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.990
Apparently the ghost asks our patients,

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.450
"When will you die?"

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.630
Oh? That's...

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.220
Hello, Nao-chan.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.140
Are you working here today?

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.140
Yes, I am.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.220
I'm currently writing up a special report on modern hospitals,

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.230
so I'll be visiting this place every so often for research purposes.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:10.650
What about you, Isshin-san?

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.860
Oh, it's nothing serious.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.990
I just have a mild headache,

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.860
so I thought I'd have it checked out.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.530
Nao, be a good a girl and wait for me until I finish my examination, okay?

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:41.300
Everything that lives will eventually die.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.350
Humans are no exception.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.560
People live to die.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.770
There's a ghost in that hospital?

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:55.940
Yes.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:02.530
Apparently, it appears in front of sleeping patients and always asks them when they will die.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:08.040
Did anything unusual happen to the patients who witnessed the ghost?

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.290
It doesn't seem like they were possessed by the ghost or anything similar.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:16.420
Although I heard that a few of the patients injured themselves while trying to get away from it.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:20.970
In addition, some of the patients' health deteriorated further as a direct result of the shock they suffered.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.180
Very well.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.680
I'll look into this matter.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.310
Please do.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.480
As it's a hospital we're talking about,

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.350
I think we better ask permission before beginning the investigation.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.440
I'll arrange it straightaway.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.860
I'll call you when everything is sorted.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.650
Oh, there's one more thing.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.370
I met Isshin-san at the hospital.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.240
You met my uncle?

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.530
Yes.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.200
He mentioned having a mild but continuous headache, so decided it'd be prudent to get it examined.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.500
I see.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:56.250
Well then, I've a prior engagement, so if you'll excuse me...

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.260
You're not going with him?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.260
I've got a club meeting to attend.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:07.260
Still, Yakumo-kun really has changed.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.560
He's become more honest...

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.350
I think he's more approachable now.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.020
He has?

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:20.150
What a coincidence that we meet here... or not, I guess.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:25.030
You're also investigating Nanase Miyuki and <i>his</i> whereabouts, and the trail led you here, correct?

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.370
Investigating is the police's job.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:31.830
Captain Miyagawa and the main investigation team are working with the Nagano Prefecture Police

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.500
in order to locate the whereabouts of the two suspects.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.920
And as usual, the two of us are-

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.800
Allowed to roam around freely with too much free time on your hands?

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.050
Yes, indeed we are.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:45.550
It's not something you should be happy about!

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.060
Sheesh, it's noisy here today.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.390
So, Sensei, why do you think you took it?

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:55.850
Well, I considered it overnight...

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.190
What are you talking about?

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:03.360
Last night, Yakumo-kun asked me...

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.950
the real reason behind why I took this photograph.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:12.160
Wasn't it because you thought he looked suspicious?

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.750
When I thought long and hard about it, there was more to it than just that.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:22.250
It was because he reminded me of something I love.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:29.720
Each human corpse leaves me with a very special impression.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:34.980
He left me with a similar impression while still being alive.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.230
And that's why I couldn't help, but...

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.440
I know!

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.570
He's the living dead!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.660
In other words, a zombie.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.620
Zom... What's that?

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:59.120
So, Yakumo's preparing himself to face his father.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:04.050
Nevertheless, he's matured a fair bit.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:09.180
That incident with Takeda Shunsuke probably helped him to take another step forward, and-

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:11.680
Idiot!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.720
Don't just stop out of the blue!

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:16.100
Not zombies, but Takeda-san!

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:21.190
The police believed that Takeda-san was the culprit, so they pursued him relentlessly.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:24.860
But in reality, he was a ghost.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:29.860
Are you saying that Yakumo's father is a ghost too?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:33.990
It can't be...

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:55.760
So... you're certain about this?

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.310
I see.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:08.190
That's a cherry tree, right?

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:10.200
Yes, it is.

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:18.290
I should take the opportunity to look at the cherry blossoms when spring arrives, right?

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:22.540
Because I most likely won't be able to do so the following spring.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:37.680
Stop!

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.020
She went that way!

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.560
Follow her!

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:41.890
Hey!

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.490
We arrested Nanase Miyuki?

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.240
That's correct.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:57.700
The Minami City Police arrested her last night.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:58.950
That's wonderful.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.460
So that just leaves Yakumo's father.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:07.130
I've sent a request in to my superiors saying that I'd like to question her.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:08.710
You're planning to meet with her?

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:16.850
In fact, the man in charge of this investigation 15 years ago is now an administrator at headquarters.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:21.730
He's trying to prevent the media from getting too interested in this incident.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:27.150
So, his reputation will be affected if the media takes an interest in this story?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.150
He did label the innocent Takeda-san as the culprit.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.990
What a bastard.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:40.740
I'd like to talk to Nanase Miyuki before that bastard can intervene.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:55.840
<i>He</i> will come for me.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.100
I'm sure of it.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:02.680
<i>He</i> will return my freedom to me again.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:11.650
Well then, Saito-san, please come back tomorrow at the same time.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.440
Of course. Thank you.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.070
Is something wrong?

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:22.910
Well, I can't seem to find my daughter who was with me when I came in.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.580
Excuse me, may I ask you something?

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.630
Did a little girl happen to wander past here?

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.970
She's a little younger than you are.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.430
Are you perhaps curious about my eye?

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:45.680
Are you scared?

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:46.810
No.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:49.190
There's nothing that scares me.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:53.070
That's reassuring to know.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:56.240
You're going to die soon, right?

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.360
And what makes you think that?

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.990
I can tell... because I shall as well.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.590
Six months remaining, eh?

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:16.010
I guess it's more or less the same for me.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:21.090
But in your case, there's still the possibility of an organ transplant.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.890
You must continue to believe in hope.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.310
But...

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:32.520
There are many people in this world who wish to donate their organs after their death.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:35.860
And that's why you must never give up.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:41.740
Mister, are you scared of dying?

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:47.540
Yes, I am, and that's despite being the chief monk of a temple.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:53.000
But it's something that will happen to everyone one day.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:56.050
What happens to you after you die?

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:59.220
There are many beliefs,

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.260
but there's not one single answer.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:04.850
Please tell me.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:08.390
Hmm... you've just handed me a great responsibility.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:24.660
Did you make that?

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.080
Yes, I did.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.910
It's my treasure.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:35.630
Now that I look at it more closely, it's even prettier.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.670
Nice vivid colors. It's really life-like.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.380
I can't believe it's actually a pressed flower.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:49.680
I made it from a flower in my garden when my parents were still getting along.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:54.060
What happens to you after you die?

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.980
Honestly, no one knows.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:09.450
But the proof of your existence lives on inside of your friends and family in the form of memories.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:15.960
Just like this flower, beautiful and life-like. An eternal reminder.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:22.970
So even if people live to die, there's still something beyond that?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.550
That's right.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:30.850
Human life has its end, but the soul lives on eternally.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.850
That's what I believe.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:38.400
That's why you're not scared to die.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.690
Of course...

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:44.530
is what I'd want to say, but actually I'm still scared.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.870
But it's okay to be scared.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:51.120
You can be scared of something scary, and sad when something is sad.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:54.290
Live your life as you feel it.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:59.920
What you absolutely must not do is to seal off your heart.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:05.880
If you do that, then that's no different from being dead.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.890
I'm scared.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:10.760
I'm scared.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:17.270
If I'm honest, I don't want to die.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.150
Good girl.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:21.900
I'm happy that you were able to admit it.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.910
Oh, Nao. Come here.

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:36.120
My name is Saito Isshin.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:39.380
This is my daughter, Nao.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.420
What's your name?

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.000
Yoshiko.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.590
Mamiya Yoshiko.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:48.390
In that case, I have a favor to ask of you.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:52.010
Will you be her friend?

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:53.310
Me?

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.720
Who are you?

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:34.970
What are you looking at?

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:39.310
The call log of the arrested Nanase Miyuki.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.150
I asked Ishii-san for it.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.270
And?

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:48.320
He checked every single number. None of them were my father's.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.370
You're slow.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:57.580
Nanase Miyuki has never talked to him over the phone.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.000
Isn't that some sort of mistake?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.670
Or... perhaps she has another cell she solely uses to call him on.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:07.010
That's a fairly good deduction coming from you.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.420
I'm honored.

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:10.090
However...

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:16.770
Ghosts do not have any physical possessions.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:21.900
Hello.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:22.900
Ozawa speaking.

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:25.570
Oh, Makoto-san.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:26.780
What?

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.280
You've obtained permission from the hospital?

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.330
Nao-chan! Long time no see.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.370
Where were you?

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.790
I was walking around the station with Nao.

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:49.130
What about yourself? Walking around with Haruka-chan?

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:51.300
I came here to ask if I could borrow your car.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:55.550
Oh? So, you're going on a drive with Haruka-chan?

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:58.010
No, it's nothing like that.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:16:01.940
Why would I go on a drive with her?

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:05.900
Oh, that's right, Makoto-san told me.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.980
How did your check-up go?

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.570
Oh, that?

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.990
I'm just overworked.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:17.200
It's because <i>someone</i> likes to worry me.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:20.120
Haruka-chan, you should take care too.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.710
I already do.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.670
Why don't we talk inside?

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.670
Come in for some tea.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:35.220
I've received a package from Keiko-san.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.720
From my mom?

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:41.770
An album?

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:45.600
She did mention that there was something she wanted to give us.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:47.230
I wonder if this is what she meant?

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.230
This one's addressed to you, Haruka-chan.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.830
Oh, this must be a photograph of your family.

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:06.790
Yes, it is.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:10.090
This was taken when my sister, Ayaka, was still alive.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:24.600
Apparently, they also exchanged photographs when they were exchanging letters.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:28.610
Then Yakumo-kun's mother must've taken these.

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:36.360
Your mother must've carefully kept the photographs she received from Asuza.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.870
He's cute!

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:50.380
He was so different from how he is now.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.380
Oh, he's finally outside.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:54.670
What?

00:17:54.670 --> 00:18:00.550
Originally, Azusa locked herself inside because of Yakumo's left eye.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:06.350
But when she realized it wasn't good, she started to go outside again.

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:10.400
That's what Keiko-san's letter says.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.900
His cheeks seem so soft! They look like marshmallows!

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:19.030
I see, so Yakumo-kun could also be like this.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:34.670
Sister...

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:37.670
So, this is Yakumo-kun's mother.

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:40.680
These must be the ones Takeda Shunsuke-san took.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.300
She has a wonderful expression.

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:49.140
I'm her brother, yet this is the first time I've seen her smiling like this.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.330
They look like a real family.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:10.830
Mother...

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:39.360
Yakumo, do you hate him? Your father.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.070
I won't tell you to stop hating,

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:48.160
but you must not let it rule you.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:51.790
Dearie me, another bad habit of mine.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.380
My stories are becoming sappy.

00:19:55.170 --> 00:20:00.800
Anyway, darkness lies in everyone.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:06.680
You need to live on by calming and persuading it.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:10.270
Why are you telling me this?

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:24.450
Because I knew I couldn't hide it from you.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:30.160
The doctor gave me a diagnosis.

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:38.670
She said I will at most have six months left.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:42.800
I want to keep it a secret from Nao.

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:44.680
Uncle...

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:52.390
Well, that's it.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:55.140
Humans' lives are short but long.

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.690
Live life as you enjoy it.

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.940
Understand, Yakumo?

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:03.700
Kill Saito Isshin...

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:05.570
Saito Isshin?

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:08.950
Bastard! You plan to harm him?

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:10.490
Not me.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:13.830
<i>He</i> will.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:28.510
Everyone lives to die.
